            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for from then on, then the Persian for recently."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: سپیده دم",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سپیده دم (sepide dam) — \"dawn, daybreak\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ما سپیده دم راه افتادیم. Mâ sepide dam râh oftâdim. We set off at dawn."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Literary; in speech sobh-e zud. sepide \"whiteness\" + dam \"breath, moment\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sepide \"whiteness, the dawn\" (EtymDB) is built on sepid \"white\", and dam here is the Persian word for \"breath, moment\": the moment of whiteness. EtymDB gives neither a parent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
