          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "شبانه روز (shabâne ruz) — \"round the clock, day and night; a full day\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "او در بیمارستان شبانه روز کار میکرد. U dar bimârestân shabâne ruz kâr mikard. She worked round the clock at the hospital."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also a noun, a full twenty-four hours: do shabâne ruz \"two days and nights\". Built from shab \"night\" with -âne and ruz \"day\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "shabâne ruz joins shabâne \"nightly\", built on shab \"night\", with ruz \"day\"; both are inherited Persian. EtymDB takes ruz back through Middle Persian to Old Persian rauča-, and sets shab beside Sanskrit kṣap- \"night\"."
            }
          ]
        },
